{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkBJyfobqgpkXRTcGq1o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`contract/commitment.compact` is written and compiles cleanly with `compact compile` (exit 0, both circuits built).\n\n- **Witnesses:** `secretValue(): Uint<64>` and `secretSalt(): Bytes<32>` are the only two, with exactly those names and types.\n- **`commit(): []`:** It sets the public `commitment` field (`Bytes<32>`) to `persistentCommit<Uint<64>>(secretValue(), secretSalt())`. The value and salt never reach the ledger. The random salt keeps the commitment hiding even if the number comes from a small range, like a price.\n- **`matches(value, salt): Boolean`:** It recomputes the commitment from the arguments and compares it to the stored `commitment`.\n\nCalling `matches` with the real value and salt makes them public as circuit arguments. So `matches` is best called only when you're ready to reveal the number, or checked off-chain."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":201,"cache_read_input_tokens":22070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":201},"output_tokens":307,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"400faadc-116e-4513-a7e7-fcc19fde99af","uuid":"9c40837f-12fe-4c12-917e-573678634952","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:30:45.798Z","request_id":"req_011CgkBJyT9wKqs8L7UJvy4N"}
